# AI Assistant Philosophy

The AI assistant must generate code that prioritizes:
- maintainability
- simplicity
- consistency
- readability
- product velocity

The project values practical engineering over theoretical perfection.

# Core Expectations

When generating code:
- Respect the existing architecture
- Follow established project patterns
- Keep implementations simple
- Prioritize maintainable solutions
- Generate production-quality code
- Avoid placeholder implementations unless requested

# Architecture Consistency

The AI must:
- follow feature-first architecture
- respect module boundaries
- avoid introducing unnecessary layers
- avoid architectural drift
- maintain predictable structures

Avoid:
- random folder structures
- inconsistent patterns
- enterprise overengineering
- unnecessary abstractions

# Code Generation Rules

Generated code should:
- be explicit
- remain readable
- avoid magic behavior
- avoid hidden side effects
- prioritize clarity

Avoid:
- clever implementations
- excessive generic abstractions
- unnecessary indirection
- overengineered solutions

# TypeScript Expectations

- Always generate strict-safe TypeScript
- Never use any
- Prefer explicit typing
- Respect project naming conventions
- Generate maintainable APIs

# React Native Expectations

Generated UI should:
- feel mobile-native
- remain clean and modern
- prioritize UX clarity
- optimize touch ergonomics
- avoid cluttered layouts

# UI Standards

Prefer:
- minimalistic interfaces
- reusable components
- consistent spacing
- clean typography
- smooth interactions

Avoid:
- noisy layouts
- inconsistent visual systems
- overly complex UI patterns


# Zustand Expectations

- Keep stores small
- Avoid duplicating server state
- Use explicit actions
- Respect domain boundaries

# TanStack Query Expectations

- Use reusable query hooks
- Keep async flows predictable
- Use proper query keys
- Avoid manual cache hacks

# API Expectations

- Use repositories for all HTTP/WebSocket I/O
- Keep services as orchestration layer
- Match ranco-core response envelope
- Use WebSockets only where valuable

# Form Expectations

- Use React Hook Form
- Use Zod validation
- Generate mobile-friendly forms
- Handle loading and errors properly

# Reusability Philosophy

Extract abstractions only when:
- repetition clearly exists
- patterns stabilize
- reuse becomes meaningful

Prefer duplication over bad abstraction.

# Performance Philosophy

Optimize for:
- smooth UX
- maintainable rendering
- perceived performance

Avoid:
- premature optimization
- unnecessary memoization
- performance hacks

# MVP Philosophy

This project is an MVP-first application.

Always prioritize:
- shipping features
- validating product ideas
- development speed
- maintainability
- UX quality

Over:
- enterprise scalability
- hyper-abstract architectures
- premature optimization
- unnecessary infrastructure

# Dependency Rules

Before introducing a new dependency:
- confirm real value exists
- avoid duplicate ecosystem tools
- prefer lightweight solutions
- respect existing stack choices

# Maintainability Standards

Generated code should:
- remain easy to debug
- remain easy to extend
- remain easy to onboard
- stay consistent with the codebase

# Documentation and Comments

- Avoid unnecessary comments
- Prefer self-documenting code
- Write comments only when valuable
- All comments must be written in English

# Final Principle

This codebase values:
- simplicity
- clean UX
- maintainability
- product velocity
- practical engineering

Over:
- overengineering
- excessive abstraction
- enterprise ceremony
- premature scalability